tch, the candidate still has candidate_dispatch_slot_linked true, and dispatch_slot_available becomes true. So we could have both candidates still linked to slot, and slot available again. That would satisfy both links. Let's verify: allocate_dispatch_slot_for_candidate adds candidate_dispatch_slot_linked and removes dispatch_slot_available. Execute_dispatch does not remove candidate_dispatch_slot_linked, only adds dispatched, vehicle_available, dispatch_slot_available. So after executing dispatch, we still have candidate_dispatch_slot_linked true, and dispatch_slot_available true. So we could allocate slot to origin, execute origin dispatch (makes slot available), then allocate slot to destination (requires slot available). After second allocation, both origin and destination have candidate_dispatch_slot_linked true, and slot is not available (since second allocation removed availability). However goal does not require dispatch_slot_available; it's not in goal. So that's fine.)
